<section id="getting-started">
<h1>Getting started <a class="lsd-anchor" href="#getting-started" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h1>
<p>Install lsdocs, create a site, and build it. Back to <a href="../index.html">home</a>.</p>
<section id="install">
<h2>Install <a class="lsd-anchor" href="#install" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h2>
<lsd-copy><figure class="lsd-code" data-language="sh"><pre class="highlight"><code class="language-sh"><span class="hl-source hl-shell hl-bash"><span class="hl-meta hl-function-call hl-shell"><span class="hl-variable hl-function hl-shell">cargo</span></span><span class="hl-meta hl-function-call hl-arguments hl-shell"> install lsdocs</span>
</span></code></pre></figure></lsd-copy>
</section>
<section id="create-a-site">
<h2>Create a site <a class="lsd-anchor" href="#create-a-site" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h2>
<ol>
<li>Run <code>lsdocs init my-docs</code>.</li>
<li>Edit <em>my-docs/docs/index.md</em>.</li>
<li>Build with <strong><code>lsdocs build</code></strong>.</li>
</ol>
</section>
<section id="build">
<h2>Build <a class="lsd-anchor" href="#build" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h2>
<p>The output goes to <code>site/</code>; <a href="configuration.html#options">Options</a> says how to change
that.
Each Markdown page becomes an HTML page;
other files are copied as they are.</p>
</section>
<section id="build-1">
<h2>Build <a class="lsd-anchor" href="#build-1" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h2>
<p>A second heading with the same title gets a unique id.
Building <span class="lsd-math lsd-math-inline">\(n\)</span> pages takes about <span class="lsd-math lsd-math-display">\[O(n)\]</span> time.</p>
</section>
</section>
